  "findings": [
    "android matches offline (same TP, FP within 1 at 0.3/0.5/0.7): preprocessing parity holds on real photos",
    "the legacy Android pipeline did not lower precision materially; it raised recall on this set (person TP 108 vs 88 at 0.5), most likely from the ~16% contrast boost of the limited-range formula and sharper nearest sampling",
    "raising the threshold from 0.5 to 0.7 did not raise precision (0.900 -> 0.885) but cut recall (0.376 -> 0.205); person precision is already 0.98 at 0.5",
    "the most persistent false positives are class confusions, not low scores: Hong Kong three-colour recycling bins also produce 'door' boxes at 0.67-0.86 that overlap the correct 'bin' box (IoU 0.95-1.00); stairs with handrails produce 'escalator' at 0.68-0.76",
    "class-agnostic NMS would not fix the bin/door case: in one image the wrong 'door' (0.86) outscores the correct 'bin' (0.79)"
  ],
  "notChanged": "no threshold or NMS change was made from this evidence; 105 mostly-person images are not enough to set per-class thresholds",
